  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/fis600.html",
  "prefLabel": "Fis 601.01 Coastal and estuarine waters",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Fis 601.01 “Coastal and estuarine waters” means all waters within the rise and fall of the tide, and water below any fishway or dam which is normally the dividing line between tide water and fresh water, or below any tidal bound which has been legally established in streams flowing into the sea under the jurisdiction of the state.\n\nSource. #745, eff 1-25-76; ss by #2263, eff 1-7-83; ss by #2839, eff 8-31-84; ss by #4868, eff 7-20-90; ss by #6291, eff 7-20-96; ss by #8087, eff 5-27-04; ss by #10095, eff 2-29-12; ss by #12652, eff 10-27-18",
